@title Borrowing FAQ
@subtitle Millbrook Public Library, effective 2026-11-01
@author Hye-jin Park, Circulation Manager

From 2026-11-01 the library stops charging late fines. Here is how borrowing works.

## Who can join the library?
Membership is free for anyone who lives, works or studies in Millbrook County. Children under 18 need a parent or guardian to sign up.

## How many items can I borrow?
You can borrow up to 30 items at once. Of those, no more than 5 can be DVDs, and no more than 2 can be Wi-Fi hotspots.

## How long can I keep things?
- Books and audiobooks: 21 days
- DVDs: 7 days
- Wi-Fi hotspots: 14 days

## What if I return something late?
There are no late fines from 2026-11-01. But an item that is 30 days overdue is treated as lost. Its replacement cost is charged, up to $25 per item.

While your account owes $10 or more, your borrowing is paused. Pay what you owe and you can borrow again.

## How do I renew?
You can renew online, in the app or at the desk, up to 3 times. You cannot renew if another reader is waiting for the item.

## How do I reserve an item?
Reservations are free. You can have up to 15 at once. A reserved item waits at the desk for 7 days after we email you.

## Questions?
Email help@millbrooklibrary.example, or visit the desk on weekdays from 09:00 to 18:00.
